  lsp_unit.pcpp - LSP compliance: the unit the other files import

  Not a test of its own. lsp_hover, lsp_definition and lsp_doc_comments
  import it to show what the editor does with a name from ANOTHER file:
  hover names this file, go to definition opens it.

  Open on its own, it must show no squiggles: a unit is checked, not built.
*******************************************************************************/

module unit lsp_unit;

/// Doubles a value.
///
/// Declared in **lsp_unit.pcpp**: hovering a use of it in another file shows
/// this text and the file name below it.
/// @param AX the value to double
/// @returns `AX` times two
exported routine Twice(const AX: int32): int32;
begin
  return AX * 2;
end;

end.
